      "connection_error_severity": "WARNING",
      "execution_error_severity": "WARNING",
      "note": "repeat_interval 72000s, matching MAINTENANCE_INDEX_FRAGMENTATION and MAINTENANCE_INDEX_USAGE, so the whole maintenance group answers for the same night and index-usage-report --days 3 always finds a run. With from_hour 1 to_hour 6 that is one run per night. The SQL uses SAMPLED mode (1% of pages), which is the expensive one, but the whole estate measured 2.9s on 2026-08-01 because no instance has a heap over 1000 pages - the cost is in the heaps found, and there are none. timeout stays 600s; revisit if a large heap ever appears.",
